From 684dff26a586b89ab7c443e268f3a6c138cabe1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mehedi Hassan <growwithmh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make category cards filter the board and let editors claim
 open work
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The workstream tiles and inventory buckets were read-only summaries, so the
only way to see one category's work was the Work dropdown, and the only way
to take a task was to open it and pick yourself from the owner list.

- inventory buckets and workstream tiles are now filter buttons; picking one
  clears the other, and clicking the pressed one clears the filter
- an Unclaimed chip counts and filters the open work nobody owns
- unassigned cards carry a Claim pill that assigns the task to the signed-in
  member in one tap, which the board, the report and My work already follow
- claiming is gated on the editor right the database enforces, so a viewer is
  never shown an action the RLS policy would refuse

The importer still only creates tasks, but it now offers — unticked, and only
to an owner or admin — to add the pages it detected to the approved inventory,
so a gated backlog import never inflates the client's approved plan.

A URL's page shape is now decided in one place, which also fixes child service
pages counting against the service-hub row when the plan has a child type.

